# Flutter Component Revision Page — `Image`

## 1. What is `Image`?

`Image` is used to **display images** in a Flutter application.

Images can come from:

* Project assets
* Internet URLs
* Device files
* Memory/data

For beginner Flutter development, the two most important types are:

```dart
Image.asset()
Image.network()
```

---

# 2. Image from Project Assets

Use `Image.asset()` when the image is stored inside your Flutter project.

```dart
Image.asset(
  "assets/images/logo.png",
)
```

Example project structure:

```text
my_app/
│
├── assets/
│   └── images/
│       └── logo.png
│
├── lib/
│   └── main.dart
│
└── pubspec.yaml
```

---

# 3. Registering Assets

Flutter needs to know about your asset folder.

In `pubspec.yaml`:

```yaml
flutter:
  assets:
    - assets/images/
```

Then run:

```bash
flutter pub get
```

Now you can use:

```dart
Image.asset(
  "assets/images/logo.png",
)
```

---

# 4. Complete Asset Example

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(
    MaterialApp(
      home: Scaffold(
        body: Center(
          child: Image.asset(
            "assets/images/logo.png",
            width: 200,
          ),
        ),
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

---

# 5. Image from Internet

Use:

```dart
Image.network()
```

Example:

```dart
Image.network(
  "https://example.com/image.jpg",
)
```

Complete example:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: Center(
    child: Image.network(
      "https://picsum.photos/300",
    ),
  ),
)
```

This downloads and displays the image from the URL.

---

# 6. Important Difference

### `Image.asset()`

```dart
Image.asset("assets/images/logo.png")
```

Image is stored **inside your application/project**.

Common uses:

* Logo
* App icons
* Background images
* Onboarding images
* Local illustrations

### `Image.network()`

```dart
Image.network("https://example.com/image.jpg")
```

Image comes from the **internet**.

Common uses:

* User profile pictures
* Product images
* News images
* Social media content
* API-provided images

---

# 7. `width` and `height`

You can control image dimensions.

```dart
Image.asset(
  "assets/images/logo.png",
  width: 200,
  height: 100,
)
```

Or:

```dart
Image.network(
  "https://picsum.photos/300",
  width: 200,
  height: 200,
)
```

---

# 8. `fit`

`fit` controls **how the image fits inside the given width and height**.

This is very important.

```dart
fit: BoxFit.cover
```

fills the available area, possibly cropping part of the image.

```dart
fit: BoxFit.contain
```

shows the entire image while maintaining its aspect ratio.

Example:

```dart
Image.network(
  "https://picsum.photos/500",
  width: 300,
  height: 200,
  fit: BoxFit.cover,
)
```

---

# 9. Important `BoxFit` Values

### `BoxFit.cover`

Fill the entire area.

```text
┌──────────────────┐
│   IMAGE IMAGE    │
│ IMAGE IMAGE      │
│    IMAGE IMAGE   │
└──────────────────┘
```

Some parts may be cropped.

Common for:

* Product cards
* Banners
* Profile backgrounds
* Thumbnails

---

### `BoxFit.contain`

Show the complete image.

```text
┌──────────────────┐
│                  │
│     IMAGE        │
│                  │
└──────────────────┘
```

The entire image remains visible.

Common for:

* Logos
* Product images
* Icons
* Documents

---

### `BoxFit.fill`

Stretches the image to exactly fit the specified size.

This can distort the image.

```dart
fit: BoxFit.fill
```

---

### `BoxFit.fitWidth`

Fits the image according to the available width.

### `BoxFit.fitHeight`

Fits the image according to the available height.

### `BoxFit.none`

Does not scale the image.

---

# 10. `Image` Inside a Container

A common pattern:

```dart
Container(
  width: 300,
  height: 200,
  child: Image.network(
    "https://picsum.photos/500",
    fit: BoxFit.cover,
  ),
)
```

The image fills the Container while maintaining its proportions.

---

# 11. Image + `Stack`

Images are frequently combined with `Stack`.

Example:

```dart
Stack(
  children: [
    Image.network(
      "https://picsum.photos/400/250",
      width: 400,
      height: 250,
      fit: BoxFit.cover,
    ),

    Positioned(
      bottom: 10,
      left: 10,
      child: Text(
        "Beautiful Place",
        style: TextStyle(
          color: Colors.white,
          fontSize: 22,
        ),
      ),
    ),
  ],
)
```

This creates:

```text
┌─────────────────────────┐
│                         │
│        IMAGE            │
│                         │
│ Beautiful Place         │
└─────────────────────────┘
```

---

# 12. Image with Rounded Corners

A common real-world design:

```dart
ClipRRect(
  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(15),
  child: Image.network(
    "https://picsum.photos/300",
    width: 300,
    height: 200,
    fit: BoxFit.cover,
  ),
)
```

`ClipRRect` clips the image into rounded corners.

---

# 13. `CircleAvatar` for Profile Images

For profile pictures, Flutter provides:

```dart
CircleAvatar()
```

Example:

```dart
CircleAvatar(
  radius: 40,
  backgroundImage: NetworkImage(
    "https://example.com/profile.jpg",
  ),
)
```

This is commonly used for:

* User profiles
* Chat lists
* Contacts
* Comments
* Account screens

---

# 14. Image Loading

For network images, Flutter needs time to download the image.

You can provide a loading builder:

```dart
Image.network(
  "https://picsum.photos/300",
  loadingBuilder: (
    context,
    child,
    loadingProgress,
  ) {
    if (loadingProgress == null) {
      return child;
    }

    return CircularProgressIndicator();
  },
)
```

The progress indicator appears while the image loads.

---

# 15. Image Error Handling

If the network image fails:

```dart
Image.network(
  "https://example.com/image.jpg",
  errorBuilder: (
    context,
    error,
    stackTrace,
  ) {
    return Icon(Icons.error);
  },
)
```

Instead of a broken image, you can show an error icon.

---

# 16. Where is `Image` Used?

You will use images in:

* Login screens
* Splash screens
* Onboarding
* E-commerce apps
* Music apps
* Social media apps
* Profile pages
* News apps
* Food delivery apps
* Product cards
* Banners
* Backgrounds

---

# 17. Quick Comparison

| Method              | Source         | Common Use              |
| ------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------- |
| `Image.asset()`     | Project        | Logo, local images      |
| `Image.network()`   | Internet       | API/user/product images |
| `CircleAvatar()`    | Circular image | Profile pictures        |
| `ClipRRect` + Image | Rounded image  | Cards/thumbnails        |

---

# 18. Most Important Code to Remember

### Local image

```dart
Image.asset(
  "assets/images/logo.png",
)
```

### Internet image

```dart
Image.network(
  "https://example.com/image.jpg",
)
```

### Resize

```dart
Image.network(
  url,
  width: 200,
  height: 150,
)
```

### Control image fitting

```dart
Image.network(
  url,
  fit: BoxFit.cover,
)
```

### Profile image

```dart
CircleAvatar(
  backgroundImage: NetworkImage(url),
)
```

---

## One-Line Definition

> **`Image` is a Flutter widget used to display images from assets, the internet, files, or other data sources.**
